   "about": "Assesses Japanese armament production, labor, wartime administration, and the economic resilience of the northern Inner Zone.",
   "summary": "The report describes weaknesses in alloy steel, precision machine tools, bearings, and skilled labor, then estimates output of aircraft, motor vehicles, and ordnance. It projects how labor could be shifted to war industries and the armed forces, and analyzes Tōjō’s efforts to centralize control of key industries. Its final chapters examine possible offensive objectives and argue that Japan was concentrating processing capacity, resources, and stockpiles in an Inner Zone comprising Japan, Korea, Manchuria, North China, and Taiwan. It concludes that losing this northern core would seriously cripple Japan’s war economy.",
